; SnowfieldTufts — Snowfield terrain visual, variant 3 of 3: the most EXPOSED. NEW 2026-09-08.
;
; 22 buried snow blades + 8 dead tufts, the most of the three, over 2 drift patches.
; Seed 20260925. The tile where wind has scoured the snow back and dead winter grass shows
; through — the counterweight to SnowfieldDrifts, so a snowfield reads as uneven cover rather
; than a uniform white sheet.
;
; BUILT BY A ONE-OFF HEADLESS SCRIPT, NOT HAND-AUTHORED — same generator, MultiMesh buffer layout
; and headless caveat as the grass-family pass; see GrassCommonShort.tscn's header. Re-run the
; generator to change anything below.
;
; INHERITS THE GRASS CALIBRATION BASELINE (human sign-off 2026-09-08): slab BoxMesh
; 1.0 x 0.2 x 1.0 at y=-0.1 (the 1.0 width is the cross-tile seam-gap fix), blotchy patches at
; y=0.001, fixed-seed scatter within +/-0.42 tile-units, +/-18% jitter, everything ground-level
; under one node named "Slab".
;
; NOTE ON "Slab": that node WAS the OcclusionFader's fade exemption. That system was removed on
; 2026-09-08 (D-59) and no code looks the name up any more — it is a grouping convention now.
;
; NO NEW ASSETS. The MegaKit ships ZERO snow content (verified across all 68 meshes and all 20
; textures), so a snow terrain cannot be sourced from the pack the rest of the family
; standardised on. The human's own proposal solved it: "take what we end up using for grass, and
; just put a blanket of snow on it." Both meshes here are already in the repo.
;
; TWO LAYERS, AND THE HEIGHT RELATIONSHIP IS THE WHOLE EFFECT:
;   - BURIED SNOW BLADES: Grass_Common_Short at scale 0.055 -> 0.073 tile-units, UNTEXTURED, flat
;     Color(0.95, 0.97, 1.0). Deliberately SHORTER than Grass's own 0.100 lawn, so they read as
;     tufts weighed down under snow rather than as white grass.
;   - DEAD TUFTS POKING THROUGH: Grass_Wispy_Short at 0.14 -> 0.150 tile-units, the scale Scrub
;     already established for that mesh. TALLER than the snow layer, which is what makes them
;     read as poking through rather than sitting on top.
;
; THE DEAD TUFTS USE THE GOLD PALETTE BAND, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. `Grass.png` is a 4-band
; palette strip; this mesh's own UVs land natively in band 1, rgb(177,152,0) gold, so it carries
; NO `uv1_offset` where every other grass scene in the project does. After the 2026-09-08 colour
; fix moved everything to band 2 (green) or band 4 (yellow-green), gold was the one band nothing
; sampled — and dead winter grass showing through snow is exactly what it is for. Do not "fix"
; the missing offset here; it is the point.
;
; UNTEXTURED WHITE IS SAFE ONLY BECAUSE THESE BLADES ARE REAL GEOMETRY at
; TRANSPARENCY_DISABLED, not alpha-cutout quads. Dropping the albedo texture off a cutout mesh
; would render solid rectangles instead of blades.
;
; ALL COLOURS, COUNTS AND SCALES ARE FIRST-PASS PROPOSALS AWAITING HUMAN SIGN-OFF.
